### **4. Real-Time Network Protocol (Optional)**
**WebSocket Integration**:
To enable real-time updates (e.g., node status, translation progress), you can use WebSockets:
- **Frontend**: Listen for updates:
  ```javascript
  const socket = new WebSocket("wss://api.pinksync.com/realtime");

  socket.onmessage = (event) => {
    console.log("Real-time update:", JSON.parse(event.data));
  };
  ```

- **Backend**: Setup WebSocket server with `ws` package:
  ```javascript
  const WebSocket = require("ws");
  const wss = new WebSocket.Server({ port: 8080 });

  wss.on("connection", (ws) => {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ message: "Welcome to PinkSync Realtime" }));
    setInterval(() => {
      ws.send(JSON.stringify({ node: "Node1", status: "online" }));
    }, 5000);
  });
  ```

